    "body": "I reworded a bit differently, in order to make it a little vaguer and sound less like it's defining something (since the actual definition is in the \"Content model\" definitions of the element).  But the important change I wanted to capture here is that an element's \"Content model\" is allowed to define both (1) constraints on the children and (2) constraints on all descendants, and these definitions are intended to be constraints on children, not constraints on all descendants.  However, the constraints do need to propagate to some descendants (`div` explicitly, and those with a transparent content model implicitly) in some cases.  (I was thinking of making an additional PR to restructure the way the `div` aspect works that I thought would be a little more questionable than this PR, so I wanted to separate it out into a second one.)\r\n\r\nWhat do you think of this rewording?",
    "created_at": "2026-05-29T14:09:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-29T14:09:18Z",
