    "body": "The reason this is better is that as it was previously written, it seemed to be excluding those things from being children rather than excluding them from being any descendant.\r\n\r\nFor example, I think the wording in the existing spec allows `<option><i><a href=\"https://example.com\">link</a></i></option>` because the content model of `<option>` allows `<i>`, and the content model of `<i>` has no restriction on interactive content.\r\n\r\nOther elements (such as `a`) clearly specify exclusions that apply to all descendants.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-29T14:41:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-29T14:41:01Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12504#discussion_r3325047323",
